  "id": "COMPOUND:19258 - PROTEIN:5032",
  "verbalization": "Isosalsoline is implicated in the biological pathway leading to DMS-79 through multiple independent routes. The first pathway links Isosalsoline to NCI-H727, which is a target of bumetanide, and ultimately to DMS-79. The second pathway connects Isosalsoline to 1,11b-Dihydro-11b-hydroxymaackiain, which targets DMS-79. The third pathway connects Isosalsoline to WiDr, which is targeted by Talosin A, also targeting DMS-79. These findings suggest that Isosalsoline may exert its effects through distinct but related mechanisms, potentially involving different molecular targets that ultimately converge on DMS-79. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with each step contributing to the overall effect on DMS-79. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Isosalsoline and DMS-79, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
